  <file id="dialogs\randomevents\xpbl\dun_cvw_hr_hopper.txt" original="dialogs\randomevents\xpbl\dun_cvw_hr_hopper.txt">
    <unit id="=&gt;q1" name="=&gt;q1">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">2</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Unlike any hopper you've seen before, this one doesn't seem to react to your close proximity, as it quietly stands still in front of the improvised prison bars. Next to the hopper is a large plate with half eaten smelly meal. The creature looks you in the eyes for a moment, before going back to finishing the plate.::

&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q2" name="=&gt;q2">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">4</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::It is likely safe to say that you may interact with the hopper now.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;a3" name="=&gt;a3">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">6</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Inspect the hopper.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q4" name="=&gt;q4">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">8</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Your knowledge of biology should be sufficient enough for you to perform a decent medical examination of this hopper. Being familiar with the base physiology of hoppers, as they are known to be some of the most fragile creatures out there, it would be advised to perform only the basic check-ups when it comes to determining the overall condition of a hopper.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q5" name="=&gt;q5">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">10</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;a6" name="=&gt;a6">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">12</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Diagnose hopper's heart condition.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q7" name="=&gt;q7">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">14</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::The lack of equipment forces you to perform only the most basic of tests. Firstly, you carefully observe the hopper's breathing pattern. After that, you gently place you hand on the hopper's body, sensing out its pulse. You use several more techniques you can quickly come up with.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q8" name="=&gt;q8">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">16</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Cardiac diagnosis points out that this hopper is in mint condition. Its heart is pumping hard and strong, and it's very clear that this creature could take on many more challenges to come.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q9" name="=&gt;q9">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">18</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Heart condition of this hopper does not stand out in any meaningful way. It's pulse is normal and there are no reasons for concern. However, knowing that this is only a hopper after all, applying additional pressure from outside sources, might push it over the edge.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q10" name="=&gt;q10">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">20</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::The diagnosis is not looking good for this one. Its heart is quite weak as irregular breathing pattern and weak pulse show little promise. Most likely caused by bad conditioning and poor overall care, this creature's coronary system is wavering, and it's only a matter of time before it stops its service.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;a11" name="=&gt;a11">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">22</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Diagnose hopper's digestive system.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q12" name="=&gt;q12">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">24</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Even for the most of the experienced biology practitioners, conclusively diagnosing the capabilities of a digestive system for a creature like hoppers, would prove to be a challenge for almost anyone in a situation like this. You start off by examining the physique of the hopper trying to find excess fat on its body that would show signs of poor metabolism. Smelling the air it exhales out may reveal traces of problems to come...::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q13" name="=&gt;q13">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">26</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::The masculine body of this hopper shows that its metabolism should be doing a great job. The fresh air it exhales and no visible abnormalities all suggest that the digestive system is exceptional and as such, it should bolster all characteristic of this creature drastically.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q14" name="=&gt;q14">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">28</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Nothing indicates that there are major issues with the digestion of this hopper. Your tests show no apparent problems nor do they point out any beneficiary exceptions that would make this hopper stand out from a regular one.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q15" name="=&gt;q15">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">30</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Excess fat hanging by the sides of the hips of this hopper, indicate possible issues with the metabolism of this creature. Its fragile legs, show noticeable asymmetry, with one having much more muscle than the other. Bad body odor and terrible smell of its exhaled breath entail a great concern for the well being of this hopper. Undoubtedly having this condition, will have negative consequences on all of the other characteristic of this animal. Feeding it with anything out of the ordinary could have grave consequences.::  &lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;a16" name="=&gt;a16">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">32</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Diagnose hopper's mental state.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q17" name="=&gt;q17">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">34</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::The mental state of these hoppers outright define the usual behavior of those, fearful creatures, which are expected to run away from almost anyone and anything they encounter. This allows you to conduct observations, previously one would find very hard to do in such environment. Focusing on the tiniest of details, some of which include the hoppers posture, eye blinking intervals, non ordinary body twitching, eye pupil movement and so forth, you assemble plenty of information.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q18" name="=&gt;q18">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">36</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Calm and collected this hopper is unusually stoic despite residing in quite, for such creatures, inhabitable environment. The mental prowess of this creature is outstanding, as it seems that it would take quite a bit to push it over the limit.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q19" name="=&gt;q19">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">38</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Your tests don't lead you to anything you would find troublesome with this creature. Everything indicates that this hopper's mental status is nominal, for whatever it's worth.:: &lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q20" name="=&gt;q20">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">40</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Bloodshot squinting eyes, twitching uncontrollably, indicate that this hopper is quite unsettled. From time to time its paws would jitter randomly, sometimes hitting nearby objects. Its closed jaw constantly dances back and forth, only settling down a bit when and if it chews food, which sometimes it outright swallows whole, choking in the process.:: &lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;a21" name="=&gt;a21">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">42</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Back.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q22" name="=&gt;q22">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">44</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::You focus closely on the hopper. Initially, you notice many little details along its fragile body. After that, you kneel down to try and spot any additional stand out characteristic, that would provide you with any useful clue about this hopper's current condition. Despite noticing many things, from which one could extract endless meaningful attributes, none of them guide you enough to formulate any concrete judgement, when it comes to figuring out the capabilities of this animal.::

&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
