        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">160</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::The hopper hesitates for a moment. Finally it decides to take a bite. Judging by its expression, the hopper seems to like it.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;a81" name="=&gt;a81">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">162</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Serve marsh honey.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q82" name="=&gt;q82">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">164</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::You place the honey on the dish.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q83" name="=&gt;q83">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">166</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::The hopper starts tasting it, tiny piece at a time. The more it eats, the faster it goes in for another taste. While digesting in, you can see the characteristic marsh honey glow shining through the hopper. Soon the entire cell glows in its light and the hopper, doesn't seem to be phased at all by it.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;a84" name="=&gt;a84">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">168</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Serve mushroom salad.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
